<div class="counseling-page">
  <section class="counseling-hero">
    <div class="container counseling-hero__inner">
      <div class="counseling-hero__copy">
        <h1>Find that<br><span class="counseling-hero__headline-main">inner peace,</span><br>finally.</h1>
        <p>Private online psychological counseling to help you understand what is weighing on you, work through old patterns, and feel more at home in your life.</p>
        <p class="counseling-hero__intro">I’m Anna Hellmuth, a medical doctor and psychologist working online with clients internationally.</p>
        <a href="{{ contact.calendar_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">{{ site.cta }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="counseling-introduction"><div class="container counseling-introduction__inner">
    <h2>Your inner world can be a place you want to live in.</h2>
    <div class="counseling-introduction__copy">
      <p>But quite often, it does not happen automatically. Especially in our modern world, we need to put effort into our wellbeing and make it a priority.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="counseling-focus bg-secondary"><div class="container">
    <div class="counseling-section-heading"><h2>Is it time to get some help?</h2><p>It is completely understandable to hesitate about seeing a mental health specialist. Nobody chooses to do so lightly. But honesty with yourself can be truly a turning point. Does anything on this list sound like you?</p></div>
    <ul class="counseling-focus__grid">
      <li>You feel anxious, emotionally exhausted, numb, or unlike yourself more often than you feel calm and present.</li>
      <li>Your relationships feel painful, lonely, or emotionally unsafe, even when you want to feel close to people.</li>
      <li>Overthinking, perfectionism, or self-criticism keep you from enjoying your life or taking the steps that matter to you.</li>
      <li>Old experiences, family patterns, or emotional burdens still influence your choices, relationships, and sense of self.</li>
      <li>Stress is showing up in your body through tension, exhaustion, difficulty sleeping, or a sense that you cannot truly rest.</li>
      <li>You are dealing with physical symptoms that doctors have identified as stress-related or psychosomatic and recommended stress management.</li>
      <li>You feel lonely and do not feel able to share your deepest pain with anyone.</li>
      <li>You have had traumatic experiences that still shape your life.</li>
      <li>You are simply unhappy, even if you cannot yet name why.</li>
      <li>You have received a diagnosis such as depression, an anxiety disorder, or post-traumatic stress disorder.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="counseling-focus__closing">Even one of these experiences can be enough reason to seek support. If several feel familiar, it’s worth taking seriously.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="counseling-outcomes" data-reveal-disabled><div class="container counseling-outcomes__inner">
    <div class="counseling-outcomes__intro"><h2>Can things really get better?</h2><p>Yes. Change is definitely possible. How far it goes is individual - for some people, life can feel dramatically better; for others, it can simply start to feel okay again. But you do not have to stay where you are now.</p></div>
    <div class="counseling-outcomes__list-wrap">
      <p class="counseling-outcomes__label">YOU CAN:</p>
      <ul class="counseling-outcomes__list">
      <li>Feel more stable, grounded, and calm in everyday life.</li>
      <li class="counseling-outcomes__featured">Recognize your patterns and respond to them with more choice.</li>
      <li>Step out of perfectionism and overthinking, and begin acting with more ease.</li>
      <li>Build relationships that feel more emotionally safe, honest, and fulfilling.</li>
      <li>Feel more at home in yourself, your body, and your life.</li>
      <li>Find your place and your people, especially after a move, loss, or major transition.</li>
      <li>Grow into making the changes your life is asking for.</li>
      <li>Enjoy and appreciate your life more fully.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="counseling-outcomes__feedback">
        <p>Some clients have shared that our work helped them feel more at ease in themselves, more honest in their relationships, and more able to make the changes they had been putting off. You can read about their experiences in their own words.</p>
        <a href="{{ page_url('home') }}#testimonials" class="btn-secondary">Read client feedback</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="counseling-sessions bg-secondary" data-reveal-disabled><div class="container counseling-sessions__inner">
    <figure class="counseling-sessions__portrait"><img src="{{ asset('images/7bc4733e-d530-4ccb-bf52-e33d3e9ac8f5.jpg') }}" alt="Anna Hellmuth seated portrait" width="800" height="1200" loading="lazy"></figure>
    <div class="counseling-sessions__copy"><h2>The essentials</h2>
      <p class="counseling-sessions__lead">The most important details about my work format.</p>
