  <section class="counseling-faq bg-secondary"><div class="container">
    <div class="counseling-section-heading"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <details class="faq-details">
      <summary>Will I need to go to counseling for years if I start?</summary>
      <p>No. Different concerns need different amounts of time. Some take longer to work through, while others can be usefully addressed in a few sessions. The rhythm and length of our work are shaped around what you need.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-details">
      <summary>How is counseling different from talking to a friend?</summary>
      <p>Your friend just listens, maybe gives you advice and compassion. A counselor also has the knowledge to see patterns, do root-cause analysis, and see the things underneath your reactions. They also possess the scientific knowledge and techniques to deal with these issues and change the patterns. So listening and compassion are just some of many things.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-details">
      <summary>How is counseling more helpful than ChatGPT or self-help books?</summary>
      <p>ChatGPT and self-help books can give you useful language, ideas, and exercises. But information alone does not automatically change an emotional pattern. You may already know exactly what you "should" do and still feel stuck. In counseling, we look at the connections underneath your reactions and the emotional weight they carry. I help you notice what is specific to your history and choose approaches that fit you, rather than offering one general answer. For now, this cannot be replaced by AI or self-help materials.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-details">
      <summary>How do I know you are the right counselor for me?</summary>
      <p>You have to listen to your feelings. It is important that you feel comfortable and safe with the specialist. If you are unsure, ask me the questions that matter to you. The discovery call exists exactly for that reason: so we can get a first feeling of whether working together is right for you.</p>
    </details>
  </div></section>

  <section class="counseling-next-step"><div class="container counseling-next-step__inner"><h2>Should I really start counseling now?</h2>
    <p>Psychological counseling is a good fit when your main need is healing-oriented: emotional burdens, anxiety, shame, attachment patterns, relationship pain, body image, burnout recovery, or the past still shaping the present.</p>
    <p>Please do not hesitate to book a discovery call or <a href="mailto:{{ contact.email }}">write me an email</a> if you have questions. I am just a human too, and I know how intimidating that first step can feel. Try not to overthink it too much.</p>
    <div class="counseling-next-step__actions">
      <a href="{{ contact.calendar_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">{{ site.cta }}</a>
      <a href="mailto:{{ contact.email }}" class="btn-secondary">Write me an email</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="counseling-disclaimer bg-dark"><div class="container counseling-disclaimer__inner">
    <p>Please note that I am based and registered in Germany. The online counseling services provided here do not constitute psychotherapy under German psychotherapy regulations. Online counseling may not be suitable for all situations. Acute psychological crises and severe mental health disorders require in-person and long-term support. In those cases, please reach out to a licensed psychotherapist or emergency services in your area.</p>
  </div></section>
